+  the device sends the previous value − 1, i.e. the largest unsigned delta, rather than a wrapped value. So −1
+  means "5.8 ms or more", not "an unknown number of wraps". The spin-down supports this: at 45.00–45.02 s the
+  deltas grow −857, −701, −534, −358, −173 as signed, which is 15,527 to 16,211 unsigned (5.50–5.74 ms), and then
+  stay at −1 (−2 seven times in the capture).
