+## What the M4 core must take from this
+
+- CC 6 is a 7-bit running tick counter: unwrap it mod 128, take the signed delta, and accept up to ±4 (seen) per
+  message. There are no sectors.
+- The pitch bend is a 14-bit timestamp at ≈ 2,822,400 Hz: unwrap it as an **unsigned** delta mod 16384 (it never
+  goes backwards), and treat −1 (16383 unsigned, and −2) as "5.8 ms or more": too slow to time (UNVERIFIED, above).
+- Speed from the timestamp works only while ticks are under 5.8 ms apart. At one tick per message that is above
+  1 / 5.805 ms = 172 ticks/s, **0.086 of 33⅓** (2000 ticks/s at 3600 ticks/rev); below that, time ticks with host arrival time.
+  M4-02's MIN_TIMED_SPEED_RATIO 0.05 is under that limit and should be checked against it.
+- Touch has to be inferred from speed; the hold phase gives the held-still signature.
